/**
 * The deterministic verification problems: published factors of safety and
 * the input that reproduces them. Generated once from the earlier per-source
 * files and kept as data; edit it by hand.
 *
 * Ids are cSlope's own. A number is one slope (its outline); a letter marks
 * a variant of it (another surface, water level, material or method). The
 * problems are ordered by the source they are checked against: published
 * literature first, by author, then the problems that come only from the
 * verification manual of a commercial slope stability program. Values from
 * such manuals are attributed to "commercial program A", "B" and so on, one
 * letter per program.
 *
 * The tolerance of each check is not written here: it follows from the
 * problem and the reference (tolerance.ts).
 */
